Q: How can Spanish Renaissance literature help us understand Latin American culture?
A: The more a person reads great literature, the more that person understands the world. The human condition is similar[ enough] throughout time[ to] be open[ to] the insight gained from literature.
Q: How does an author’s use[ of] language affect the way you translate?
A: If a[ writer] is using an elaborate, baroque style…or a very clean, spare style, I do my best to write that kind of English. I’m trying to allow the reader in English to experience the text in a way that’s comparable to the way the Spanish-language reader experiences it.
